Subject: WPE on Phoenix: Media Source Extensions over the FFmpeg media player's decoders

MediaSource and SourceBuffer (hls.js, dash.js, Shaka, video.js-VHS) without GStreamer
(coordination repo docs/browser/MSE-DESIGN.md, stage 1), on top of patches 0030/0031
(platform/graphics/ffmpeg/, BSD-2-Clause), with ENABLE_MEDIA_SOURCE:

  MediaPlayerPrivateFFmpegMSE   a second engine (FFmpegMSE), chosen only for MediaSource loads:
                                readyState, duration, buffered and seekable are WebCore's
                                MediaSource's; a seek waits for the target to be buffered
                                (waitForTarget), then WebCore flushes and enqueues every track from
                                the sync frame before it (MockMediaPlayerMediaSource's pattern); the
                                clock runs from HaveFutureData on and holds below it ('waiting');
                                the decoders open at the first play()
  MediaSourcePrivateFFmpeg      creates the SourceBuffers; the first track of each kind feeds the
                                engine's one video and one audio input
  SourceBufferPrivateFFmpeg     appends parsed on the dispatcher (the main thread: the parser walks
                                boxes, it decodes nothing), one MediaSampleFFmpeg per coded frame;
                                WebCore's TrackBuffers do coded frame processing, eviction and the
                                buffered ranges; enqueued frames go to the engine; buffer limit
                                40 MB video / 8 MB audio, 8 / 2 MB before the first play
  MediaSampleFFmpeg             a coded frame: an AVPacket (padded copy of the payload, shared by
                                the sample's copies), MediaTimes in the track's timescale, its
                                FFmpegCodecConfig; non-displaying frames go to the decoder with
                                AV_PKT_FLAG_DISCARD (decoded for reference, never returned)
  FFmpegFMP4Parser              plain C++ (host-tested against FFmpeg's mov demuxer): the ISO BMFF
                                byte stream format, split anywhere across appends; moov (avc1/avc3,
                                hvc1/hev1, mp4a, Opus, ac-3, ec-3, fLaC), moof/traf/tfhd/tfdt/trun,
                                the edit list as the mov demuxer applies it; encrypted tracks and
                                explicit base-data-offsets refused
  FFmpegPlaybackEngine          the decode/present/sound threads for frames that arrive demuxed:
                                0030's picture path (compositor upload, CPU conversion of other
                                formats, late drop), its /dev/audio0 writer (the same lock file:
                                one writer), a pausable clock held at start, seek and stall; a
                                frame with a new configuration (quality or codec switch) drains and
                                reopens the decoder; HEVC goes to hevc_rpivid. Written for MSE; the
                                progressive/HLS player keeps its own threads for now.

Type answers (MediaSource.isTypeSupported, addSourceBuffer, changeType; they steer adaptive
players): video/mp4 and audio/mp4 only; HEVC Main/Main10 up to level 4.1
(WPE_PHOENIX_MSE_HEVC_4K=1: any); H.264 up to level 3.1, 720p30 (WPE_PHOENIX_MSE_H264_1080=1: up
to 4.2); AAC, MP3, Opus, AC-3, E-AC-3, FLAC; width/height/framerate parameters held to the same
limits; no WebM, MPEG-TS, VP9, AV1 or encrypted media. MediaCapabilities media-source answers use
the MSE engine's containers.

Plumbing: MediaPlatformType::FFmpeg, MediaPlayerType::FFmpegMSE,
MediaPlayerMediaEngineIdentifier::FFmpegMSE (+ its IPC serialization and the remote player's
switch), MediaSample::Type::FFmpegSample and a const AVPacket* PlatformSample, the engine's
registration under USE(FFMPEG) && ENABLE(MEDIA_SOURCE), the sources in platform/FFmpeg.cmake.

Logs ("WPEB-MEDIA ... id=<n> ..."; MSE players count from 1001): canplaytype type= platform=media-source
answer= engine=mse reason=, mse load/addsourcebuffer/init tracks= video= audio= generation=/track/
append bytes= samples=/append-error/reset-parser/changetype/plays/track-ended/ready-state/seek/
seek done pts=/end-of-stream/size/stall, decoder video|audio=<name> config=, decoder reopen,
first-frame, first-sound, drained, end, and the stat line (decoded presented painted dropped fps
av_ms hw ready stalls q_kb mse_sb mse_kb mse_samples played players).

